  "configuration_id": "config_015",
  "reason": "Evidence: All completed experiments used imagenet_vit_l as the image encoder, so the image representation choice is completely unexplored. The RNA encoder (scvi_n200 vs pca_n2000) and profile setting (multi vs single) have been shown to matter substantially, but we have no information on whether a lighter image encoder (resnet50) is competitive or a bottleneck. Question: config_015 (scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) differs from config_049 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat, acc=0.715) in exactly one variable—the image encoder—making it a clean single-factor comparison. Why best next experiment: Under a limited budget, isolating the image encoder effect is critical because it determines whether we should continue investing in the larger ViT-L backbone or whether a simpler encoder suffices. If resnet50 is competitive, it tells us the image representation is not the current bottleneck and we should focus on RNA encoder (e.g., scgpt) or fusion details; if it degrades significantly, it confirms imagenet_vit_l is essential and justifies keeping it in all future configurations. This single experiment reduces uncertainty about a major untested design axis without confounding multiple changes."
}

